        "paragraphs": [
          "Learned settings are the weights and offsets a model adjusts. An executable program also saves the computation using them and the input rules needed to run it. This action produces an inference package rather than a training checkpoint.",
          "Static batch accepts one declared observation count. Bounded batch accepts a minimum-to-maximum count while each observation keeps the same input fields. The chosen CPU or Apple GPU device is explicit; a mismatch refuses instead of silently switching.",
          "Check the real saved-and-reloaded results, actual size-boundary refusals, isolated portable-helper execution and changed-byte or stale-signature rejection. Reloading executes computation: only open trusted app-generated programs. Whole-bag packet models use their existing trained inference export."
        ]
